 ## Background
-Volume SDF Rendering is a technique used in neural rendering to combine the benefits of implicit surface representations (SDFs) with volume rendering. It was popularized in the context of fitting neural surfaces from multi-view images, such as in the VolSDF method [S5, unofficial]. The approach converts the signed distance field into a density field using a probabilistic model (Laplace distribution CDF) to allow standard volume rendering integrals to capture the surface appearance [S1, unofficial]. It is widely used in academic projects and implementations for neural surface reconstruction and rendering, such as those found in CMU's Learning for 3D Vision course assignments [S5, unofficial].
